# Allowlist: exclude everything, then un-exclude only what the cargo build needs.
# A minimal, stable build context keeps the StageX image reproducible (stray local
# files - datadirs, cookies, target/ - can never leak into the build).
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!src
!rose-cli
# A workspace member must be in the context or cargo refuses to load the workspace; the
# image builds only the two daemon-side binaries from it.
!rose-petal
# `example-config` embeds this with include_str!, so the build needs it in the context.
!rose.example.toml
# License texts shipped in the runtime image (rose is statically linked, so the
# third-party notices must travel with the binary). THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt is also a
# *build* input: src/licenses.rs embeds it with include_str! for `rose licenses`, so
# dropping it from this allowlist breaks the compile, not just the runtime COPY.
!LICENSE-MIT
!LICENSE-APACHE
!THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt
# The enclave stage's default bake tree: empty but for its placeholder, so the default
# build bakes nothing. A deployment passes its own with --build-arg ROSE_BAKE.
!deploy/bake
